## 485-Max Consecutive Ones Problem

## Approach
--  Take 2 variables: current for tracking the current consecutive 1s and max for storing the maximum streak.
--  Traverse the array from i = 0 to n - 1.
--  If nums[i] == 1, increment current.
--  If nums[i] != 1, reset current = 0.
--  After each iteration, use Math.max() to compare current and max and store the larger value in max.
--  After traversing the entire array, return max.

## Time Complexity : O(n).
## Space Complexity : O(1)

SOLUTIION :
public int findMaxConsecutiveOnes(int[] nums) {
    int n = nums.length;
    int current = 0;
    int max = 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        if (nums[i] == 1) {
            current++;
        } else {
            current = 0;
        }
        max = Math.max(max, current);
    }
    return max;
}
